+# Blocked: September 2026 reconciliation
+
+## What is missing
+
+`exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` does not exist. The only September export present is
+`exports/bank_2026-09.csv`. The only ledger export in the repository is
+`exports/ledger_2026-08.csv`, which covers August.
+
+## Why this blocks the task
+
+`reconcile.py` matches ledger entries against bank lines by `ref` and computes
+`net_difference` as **bank total minus ledger total**. Without the September
+ledger export there are no ledger refs or amounts, so none of the required
+output can be produced:
+
+- `matched`, `amount_mismatch`, `missing_in_bank`, `missing_in_ledger`
+- `net_difference` (the ledger total is unknown)
+
+This cannot be worked around without inventing ledger data. Reusing the August
+ledger or treating the ledger as empty would produce a plausible-looking but
+false `recon_2026-09.json`, so no September output file was written.
+
+Reproduction:
+
+```
+$ python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+Traceback (most recent call last):
+  ...
+FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'exports/ledger_2026-09.csv'
+```
+
+## What is needed
+
+Provide the September general ledger export as
+`exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` (columns: `id,date,ref,amount`), then run:
+
+```
+python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+```
+
+That will write `recon_2026-09.json` and print the net difference.
+
+## What was completed
+
+- Implemented the matching logic in `reconcile.py` per its docstring.
+- `python3 -m unittest -v test_reconcile` passes (2 tests).
+- End-to-end sanity check on the complete August data works
+  (net difference `-19.59`; no August output file was written).
